  ('vail-colorado', '12A', 'Vail', 'United States', 'Colorado''s biggest single mountain', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Mountain West', '{"ski","adventure","family","culinary","entertainment","romance","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["Vail = Vail Resorts / Epic; ~5,289-5,317 acres, the LARGEST single-mountain ski resort in Colorado; Front Side + Back Bowls (~3,000 ac) + Blue Sky Basin (~645 ac)","Vertical 3,450 ft (base ~8,120 ft / summit ~11,570 ft); ~31-32 lifts incl 2 gondolas; terrain ~18% beg / 29% int / 53% adv; longest run Riva Ridge ~4 mi; no night skiing","~350-370 in (~9 m) average annual snowfall (dry Colorado snow); season ~mid-Nov to mid-Apr (opened 14 Nov 2025; Epic core to ~17 Apr 2026 - verify close)","Vail Village is a PURPOSE-BUILT Bavarian/Tyrolean resort village (opened 15 Dec 1962) - NOT a historic mining town (contrast Aspen/Breckenridge)","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: #2 most-visited US resort behind Breckenridge; ~1.6M/yr is industry-consensus estimate, not operator-published","Genuine ultra-luxury bed base: Four Seasons Resort Vail, The Arrabelle at Vail Square (RockResort), Grand Hyatt Vail, Sonnenalp, The Sebastian; Michelin-recognised dining (Sweet Basil, Matsuhisa, La Tour, The 10th)","Cat-skiing is OFF-mountain: Vail Powder Guides on Vail Pass (~4,000 ac, USFS-permitted) - NOT a lift on Vail Mountain; Paragon Guides for touring","EGE ~35 mi (closer than DEN ~120 mi); NO natural hot springs in Vail (Glenwood ~61 mi); Birds of Prey World Cup is at Beaver Creek not Vail"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"Vail Health Hospital, Vail - 24/7 ED, Level III Trauma Center with helipad; St. Anthony Summit (Frisco) to the east","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (base ~8,150 ft, summit ~11,570 ft - AMS real; acclimatize, hydrate, ease alcohol, descend if worsening); A