  ('winter-park-colorado', '12A', 'Winter Park', 'United States', 'Denver''s closest big mountain', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Mountain West', '{"ski","adventure","family","culinary","entertainment","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Winter Park = City & County of Denver-owned, Alterra-operated / Ikon; Colorado''s longest continuously-operating resort (since 1939-40); Denver''s closest major (~67 mi via US-40/Berthoud Pass)","Seven territories incl. Mary Jane (legendary ungroomed moguls, opened 1975) + Parsenn Bowl + the extreme Vasquez Cirque; ~3,081 acres (1,212 off-piste), 171 trails, vertical 3,060 ft (base 9,000 / summit 12,060), 23 lifts + 10-person gondola","~344.6 in (~8.75 m) snowfall; steep split ~8 beg/18 int/19 adv/52 most-difficult/3 expert-only; longest run 4.9 mi (Parsenn Bowl); no night skiing","The Winter Park Express - Amtrak SKI TRAIN from Denver Union Station to a ski-in platform (57 round trips 2025-26; Thu-Sun + holidays via Moffat Tunnel)","NSCD (National Sports Center for the Disabled) based here since 1970 - one of the world''s largest adaptive-sport orgs, deep Paralympic-medal legacy","BACKCOUNTRY: NO powder cat-skiing at the resort - Vasquez Cirque is hike-to / Cirque-Sled transport (boundary aid, not guided cat-ski); off-resort cat via Jones Pass Guides; Berthoud Pass hike-to BC","Lodging is CONDO/mid-range, NOT 5-star flags - a value, less-crowded alternative to the Vail/Summit corridor; NO natural hot springs on-site (Hot Sulphur ~27-31 mi)","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: heavy Front-Range volume by consensus, not published; CAIC ''Front Range'' zone; Middle Park Health Fraser campus (24/7 ER, opened Jun 2025)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"Middle Park Health - Fraser campus (Winter Park/Fraser border, opened Jun 2025) - 24/7 ER, trauma bays, helipad; Granby (surgical) + Kremmling (Level IV trauma) other campuses","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (base ~9,000 ft, summit 12,060 ft - AMS real; acclimatize, hydrate, descend if worsening); AVALANCHE out-of-bounds gates + Berthoud Pass - CAIC ''Front Range'' zone daily bulletin (by ~4:30 PM, includes Berthoud Pass), beacon/probe/shovel + guide, never duck ropes (Vasquez Cirque in-bounds is patrolled); tree-wells (Mary Jane); cold + unforgiving bumps; US-40/Berthoud Pass winter driving + Traction/Chain Law - check CDOT cotrip.org","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","read":"2026-08-20T14:47:42Z","page_updated":"2026-08-18T10:29:04+01:00","source_country":"usa","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter (Christmas/NY, MLK, Presidents'', Feb-Mar) + every powder weekend (Denver day-trippers); ski-train Thu-Sun concentrates weekend demand","shoulder":"early season (late Nov-mid Dec), Jan midweek, April spring skiing","green":"May-Jun + Oct-Nov lull; summer bike park + festivals","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' + powder weekends 2-5 mo; ski-in/out condos 3-6 mo; midweek/shoulder 1-4 wk; Ikon lowest spring on-sale","off_season_specials":"midweek value; April spring skiing; ski-train packages; summer bike-park + festivals","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, MLK + Presidents'', spring break; ski-train weekends; summer festivals (verify dates)","fire_date":"FIRE spring early-bird (Apr-Jun) Ikon on-sale + ski-train pre-sell; fire again Sep-Nov leaning on Denver-proximity + ski-train + Mary-Jane bumps"},"jewels":[{"name":"Ride the ski train to the Mary Jane bumps","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"Ikon/dynamic ticket; package + train far better value","timing":"ski Dec-Apr; ski-train Thu-Sun + holidays","draw_rank":1,"hook":"arrive by Amtrak at a ski-in platform, then ski the